 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "When this monument in Mexico City opened in 1910, you walked straight up to it.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Today you need to climb fourteen extra steps. The monument didn't grow. The city sank.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The city was built on top of an old lake. Under the streets is soft clay full of water.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Millions of people pump their drinking water from wells under that clay.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "As the water leaves, the clay dries out and squeezes together, like a sponge.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So the ground and everything on it slowly drops. In some places, almost an inch every month.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But the monument stands on piles that go down to firm ground, so it stays put.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The street drops around it, and every few years, workers add another step.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The monument is fine. The city is the one going down. Now you know.",
   "pausa": 0.2
  }
 ],
